ValveResourceFormat (Source 2 Viewer)
https://github.com/ValveResourceFormat/ValveResourceFormat

Derived from it:

- src/material/inputs.rs: the table of which inputs the channels of each shader's texture
  parameters hold (the shaders' names, the texture parameters' names and the channels'
  input names), and the glTF slots with the inputs each takes. The rules that match a
  shader's inputs to a slot follow the project's too. The table is in the project's
  ValveResourceFormat/IO/ShaderDataProvider.cs.
- src/material/convert.rs: the constants and the error correction of the sRGB to linear
  conversion (`srgb_to_linear`), from the project's ColorSpace.SrgbGammaToLinear.

Everything else that mentions the project (the glTF exports of materials, clips, vertex
attributes and worlds; the sprite sheet crop; the normal map reconstruction; the semantics of
a few particle operators) is heatel's own code, written to give the same results as the
project's output or behaviour; it is not a transcription of the project's code.

